# Symbol picker source, read by `varia symbols`. One entry per line:
# character, space, description. Lines beginning with # and blank lines are
# ignored. Matching is fuzzy against the whole line, so descriptions act as
# search terms.
#
# Characters here are non-ASCII by definition. If an entry stops working after
# an edit, check it was not flattened to ASCII on the way in:
#   grep -v '^#\|^$' FILE | LC_ALL=C grep -n '^[[:print:]] '

